---
description: Ban basedpyright reportAny and reportExplicitAny in Python; type managers and dicts without Any
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: true
---

# basedpyright: no `Any`

Do not write Python that triggers **`reportAny`** or **`reportExplicitAny`**. Do not use `typing.Any`,
`from typing import Any`, `dict[str, Any]`, `list[Any]`, `*args: Any`, `manager: Any`, or
`# type: ignore` / `# pyright: ignore` to hide those rules.

**Enforced since #784.** After editing Python, run `uv run basedpyright` (full run, no file arguments)
from the repo root. It exits non-zero on any finding not already in `.basedpyright/baseline.json`.
The same check runs in pre-commit, in CI, and via `make typecheck`.

Deleting an annotation to dodge the rule does not work either: an unannotated parameter fires
`reportMissingParameterType` / `reportUnknownParameterType`, which are gated too. `Unknown` is
simply the implicit form of `Any`.

**Never run `basedpyright --writebaseline` to silence a new finding.** The baseline may only shrink;
`make any-report` shows what remains. A genuinely correct suppression must name its rule and carry
`# Reason: <CATEGORY> - <cause>` plus `# Appropriate because: <why Any is right, ≥40 chars>`
(enforced by `scripts/lint_pyright_suppressions.py`). Full rules: **No `Any` in `server/` (enforced)**
in `AGENTS.md`.

## Ponytail / shortest-diff

`typing.Any` is **not** a lazy shortcut. It fails basedpyright and gets rewritten, so it is the
_longest_ path. Protocol + TypedDict (matching real dict value types) is the shortest _correct_
diff. Never hide `reportAny` / `reportExplicitAny` with `# type: ignore` or `# pyright: ignore`.

## Fixes (use these, not `Any`)

- **Structured dicts:** `TypedDict` (see `NewGameSessionResult` in `connection_session_management.py`).
- **Cross-module manager/helpers:** a `Protocol` whose **mutable dict value types match the real class
  exactly**. `dict[str, WebSocket | None]` is not assignable to `dict[str, WebSocket]` (invariance).
- **Cycles:** do **not** `TYPE_CHECKING`-import `ConnectionManager` from a module that
  `connection_manager.py` already imports (`reportImportCycles`). Use a Protocol instead.
- **Tests:** typed locals, e.g. `svc: AsyncMock = AsyncMock()`, not file-level `reportAny` suppression.

```python
# BAD
from typing import Any
async def handle(..., manager: Any) -> dict[str, Any]: ...

# GOOD
class _SessionConnectionManager(Protocol):
    active_websockets: dict[str, WebSocket]
    player_sessions: dict[uuid.UUID, str]
    # ...same types as ConnectionManager...

class NewGameSessionResult(TypedDict):
    success: bool
    errors: list[str]

async def handle(..., manager: _SessionConnectionManager) -> NewGameSessionResult: ...
```
